From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mountmgr: only UDisks2's own signals, not every PropertiesChanged on the system bus

mountmgr's UDisks2 match rule for PropertiesChanged named no sender, so every
winedevice.exe got every PropertiesChanged signal on the system bus: systemd
sends several for each unit it starts and stops (on a desktop with
socket-activated services, tens of thousands a day). A winedevice.exe that
stopped reading -- hung, or left behind when its wineserver went away --
kept them queued; at 128 MB the bus stopped reading from systemd itself, and
every systemctl, systemd-run and login that asks systemd over D-Bus timed
out (host 2026-11-27: three leftover test winedevice.exe held 133 MB each,
systemd-run --user --scope failed with "Connection timed out").

Both UDisks2 rules now name UDisks2 as the sender; the PropertiesChanged one
is also limited to that signal under /org/freedesktop/UDisks2. The Bluetooth
driver's rules already name BlueZ.

diff -ru a/dlls/mountmgr.sys/dbus.c b/dlls/mountmgr.sys/dbus.c
--- a/dlls/mountmgr.sys/dbus.c	2026-11-27 18:35:42.180236540 -0800
+++ b/dlls/mountmgr.sys/dbus.c	2026-11-27 18:35:42.192236462 -0800
@@ -551,11 +551,19 @@
     static const char udisks_match[] = "type='signal',"
                                        "interface='org.freedesktop.UDisks',"
                                        "sender='org.freedesktop.UDisks'";
+    /* only UDisks2's own signals: with no sender, every PropertiesChanged on
+     * the system bus came here -- systemd's for each unit started -- and a
+     * winedevice.exe that stops reading (hung, its wineserver gone) let them
+     * pile up until the bus stopped reading systemd itself */
     static const char udisks2_match_interfaces[] = "type='signal',"
+                                                   "sender='org.freedesktop.UDisks2',"
                                                    "interface='org.freedesktop.DBus.ObjectManager',"
                                                    "path='/org/freedesktop/UDisks2'";
     static const char udisks2_match_properties[] = "type='signal',"
-                                                   "interface='org.freedesktop.DBus.Properties'";
+                                                   "sender='org.freedesktop.UDisks2',"
+                                                   "interface='org.freedesktop.DBus.Properties',"
+                                                   "member='PropertiesChanged',"
+                                                   "path_namespace='/org/freedesktop/UDisks2'";
 
 
     DBusError error;
